WEBVTT

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:01.800
It is the period of warring states.

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:03.440
The era of competing warlords.

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:08.320
Among them, Oda Nobunaga was only a 
short step away from seizing total power.

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:08.320
Oda Nobunaga

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:12.990
But he was taken down at Honnou-ji by the betrayal of his vassal, Akechi Mitsuhide.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:13.000
Akechi           Mitsuhide

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:18.490
After that, Toyotomi Hideyoshi reached east, 
continuing his momentum towards total conquest.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:15.000
Toyotomi Hideyoshi

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:17.120
Takenaka         Hanbei

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:22.500
But like Nobunaga, he was confronted by the 
betrayal of a subordinate, Tokugawa Ieyasu.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.000
Lord Hideyoshi, I will defeat you!

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.880
Ieyasu!

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:32.020
I swear I'll kill you!

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:34.970
Ieyasu!

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:48.570
<b>It is almost two point
five decades since I was born</b>

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:50.950
<b>I've had so many of jellos so far</b>

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.740
<b>and how many more will I swallow from now on?</b>

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:57.200
<b>I've already taken tons of exams</b>

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:59.660
<b>and what else is coming up to me from now on?</b>

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:02.830
<b>Daily lives must pass by quickly
without any "likes" and "hates"</b>

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:04.500
<b>That girl who falls for guys easily,</b>

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.960
<b>fell for another one then another
one and another one each time</b>

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:08.380
<b>For a guy without such experience</b>

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:12.630
<b>Everyday life now is like a stormy river</b>

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:13.840
<b>So fast!</b>

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:18.140
<b>Break out!</b>

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:26.520
<b>(so) I sing to myself before I get sunk</b>

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:31.400
<b>I jumped out to stop the streaming days</b>

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:37.950
<b>The coastline I ran on that strong sunny day
(Shore line I ran)</b>

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:42.620
<b>If you wanna take back that feeling
(take back that feeling)</b>

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:46.880
<b>That feeling and give it a deep color of your own self
(take back that feeling)</b>

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:49.800
<b>First, smash down that door</b>

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:03.000
You're the only man who can set me on fire!

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:10.570
Magnum Step!

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:14.450
<i>(Flare Storm)</i>

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:14.450
Rekka!

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:14.700
Rekka

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:14.700
Rekka

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:20.450
And I have seen true strength in you!

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:42.350
Don't break formation!

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:43.940
Charge through the enemy's right flank!

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:51.800
Turbulent Times

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:53.960
Oyakata-sama!

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:55.520
Major news! {how to make this more formal}

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:57.690
Oyakata-sama! There's news—

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:58.680
Quiet!

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.600
Don't be rash, Yukimura.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:04.950
B-But...

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:09.320
According to Sasuke, Toyotomi was killed in action at Odawara—

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:10.370
I know.

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:13.580
An old friend informed me.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:16.610
Old... friend?

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:21.550
I'm Shimazu Yoshihiro of Satsuma.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:25.470
I've known Shingen of Takeda for a long time.  {please check all this guys' dialog because his dialect is so thick}

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:27.990
I... I apologize for not recognizing you.

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:28.970
My name is—

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:31.980
Sanada Genjirou Yukimura.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:34.610
I've heard quite a lot about you.

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:36.480
Shimazu         Yoshihiro

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:39.660
Oh, I've intruded upon your meeting!

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:44.780
Yer one lucky guy.

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:47.590
You've got a young one to entrust the future to.

00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:50.750
I haven't taught him everything yet— {or is he saying, he hasnt told Yukimura anythingyet?}{tsutaeru as in pass down his wisdom/knowledge to yukimura so that he's ready to succeed him.}

00:03:54.350 --> 00:03:55.510
Sasuke!

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:59.000
You should have told me we had a guest!

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:00.400
Not my fault.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:04.070
You just barged in without properly listening to me.

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:08.710
Still, I can't believe that Tokugawa Ieyasu would start a rebellion.

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:13.570
He's Tokugawa Ieyasu. It doesn't really surprise me. {wtf is this upposed to mean}{he's basically saying he can understand why tokugawa would. that he would stand up for his principles inferring from the first ep, but i don't want to spell it out too much}

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:17.330
Ieyasu!

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:19.020
Osaka Castle

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:25.000
Ieyasu...

00:04:34.070 --> 00:04:37.600
Hideyoshi-sama, Hanbei-sama,

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:41.130
please, order me!

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:45.360
Command me to die. {*is that right}{yes. he'd rather die at this point}

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:47.630
Mitsunari.

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:50.500
<i>You</i> are now the master of this castle.

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:53.230
What are you saying, Gyoubu?

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:58.230
The only one who can lead the Toyotomi and rule this nation is Hideyoshi-sama!

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:04.240
If so, you certainly cannot overlook Tokugawa,

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:09.220
who is mobilizing his troops to bring the Land of the Rising Sun under his rule.{*is that right}{せんと is like しようと, also 兵を進める}

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:11.040
Ieyasu...?

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:14.510
He has not only killed our lord,

00:05:14.510 --> 00:05:18.690
but also plans to overtake Toyotomi's dominant position among those vying for total conquest.

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:20.500
What...?

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:24.050
I won't allow it!

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:27.620
I won't forgive such actions!{そのような所業}

00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:30.430
That's right, Mitsunari.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:37.480
While he prattles about bonds, he's absorbed the 
Houjou remnants and is steadily growing in power.

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:43.030
The man who betrayed Hideyoshi-sama has no right to speak of bonds!

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:46.370
<i>Victory goes to the Toyotomi.</i>

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:48.780
<i>Don't overdo it, Mitsunari.</i>

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:57.970
If you keep fighting like this, your body won't last.

00:05:57.970 --> 00:05:59.740
What are you saying?

00:05:59.740 --> 00:06:02.770
I live for Hideyoshi-sama's sake.

00:06:02.770 --> 00:06:04.710
Don't you?

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:10.100
I believe in the nation that Lord Hideyoshi is trying to create.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:11.280
And...

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:12.430
<i>Shut up!</i>

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:15.700
in my bond with Lord Hideyoshi.

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:16.680
<i>Shut up!</i>

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:20.190
Shut up, Ieyasu!

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:33.330
It's all because... of my foolishness.

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:37.080
Because I trusted Ieyasu that day.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:40.680
Hideyoshi-sama, Hanbei-sama...

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:46.590
Please let me forget the memory of my foolishness on that day!

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:48.870
<i>Mitsunari.</i>

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:57.900
<i>Our lord's death, Tokugawa's betrayal...</i>

00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:00.990
<i>It has killed you while leaving you alive.</i>

00:07:00.990 --> 00:07:06.780
<i>Why are you still in pain? Why do you still suffer?</i>

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:10.860
Hideyoshi... sama...

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:13.350
Lord Shingen.

00:07:13.350 --> 00:07:14.560
My teacher.

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:17.620
Mikatagahara

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:27.170
When I was young, I lost a battle to you here, and learned much.

00:07:27.820 --> 00:07:30.120
Now is the time to show you what I learned.

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:33.120
Ieyasu, he made you suffer back then.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:38.620
I always believed you would return the favor one day, here at Mikatagahara{place name}.

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:41.690
But our objective is not to win against the Takeda.

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:45.200
I believe I can form a bond with the Takeda.

00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:49.380
For that purpose, I need to show it to Lord Shingen.

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:53.200
The power of my bonds!

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:02.520
So, they're coming.

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:04.710
Excuse me, my lord!

00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:09.140
Tokugawa Ieyasu's army is headed to our territory, to Mikatagahara!{i dunno the rest of this*}

00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:10.010
What?!

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:11.580
Oyakata-sama!

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:15.520
Let's go, Yukimura.

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:17.740
Oyakata-sama...

00:08:17.740 --> 00:08:19.910
Ieyasu has come.

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:22.730
H-How did you know?!

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:25.250
His presence.

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:28.360
I felt the presence of a tiger.

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:34.910
<i>They pursued us relentlessly. {how do i get in iya}</i>

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:37.640
<i>Thanks to that, I have no idea where we are.</i>

00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:57.200
Another ambush?

00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:59.160
No, it's Uesugi.

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:04.470
At some point, we were chased into the 
territory of Uesugi, Echigo's God of War.

00:09:04.470 --> 00:09:06.620
We've been tricked by Toyotomi.

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:09.020
A god of war lives here.

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:14.280
It is not a place where a shattered dragon should come. {is there a bettre wording for this}{shattered?}

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:16.450
Uesugi       Kenshin

00:09:28.280 --> 00:09:29.750
Ieyasu.

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:31.920
That's an impressive battle formation. {is this right?}{見事な陣構え — impressive battle formation.}

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:35.000
Looks like I was right to come visit you.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:37.680
I wouldn't find such an enjoyable battlefield anywhere else.

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:39.660
I'm going out there!

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:41.430
Let us meet again.

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:44.120
Right.

00:09:56.840 --> 00:09:58.710
Lord Uesugi Kenshin!

00:09:58.710 --> 00:10:04.070
We are here only because we were 
attacked and pursued into this territory.

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:06.450
I beg you!{naritazo?}{nani dozo}

00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:10.530
Please overlook this one intrusion.

00:10:10.530 --> 00:10:11.960
Overlook?

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:16.540
In this world of war, you would ask me to let a wounded rabbit go?

00:10:16.540 --> 00:10:19.970
That kind of optimism does not befit a soldier like you.

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:23.470
Heh, that's for sure.

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:29.410
I can't believe that I, the Dragon's Right Eye, would forsake my dragon's pride!

00:10:29.410 --> 00:10:32.980
I'm so ashamed that I could slay myself right now!

00:10:33.490 --> 00:10:36.030
And that will atone for your actions?

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:38.070
Of course it won't.

00:10:40.170 --> 00:10:42.850
I will clear my own name. {i'm kinda being liberal but i want this to make sense, does it make sense?}

00:10:42.850 --> 00:10:45.200
God of War, Uesugi Kenshin!

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:48.710
I will strike you down, and pass through!

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:53.520
Sanada Genjirou Yukimura!

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:55.340
I will head to the front!

00:10:57.260 --> 00:10:58.400
I've told you...

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:01.430
When you're going to lead a charge, at least tell me first!

00:11:15.870 --> 00:11:18.030
As expected of Tokugawa-dono.

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:19.520
His troops are not easily defeated. {一筋縄ではいかない}

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:24.120
Even so, aren't our soldiers falling back a <i>bit</i> too much?

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:26.990
That's...

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:29.460
The yellow smoke signal for emergencies!

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:32.400
Sasuke!

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:33.580
I will leave this to you!

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:34.900
I'll return shortly!

00:11:47.420 --> 00:11:48.960
<i>He has no openings at all.</i>

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:52.940
<i>And, I'll get a single hit on him at most.</i>

00:11:53.310 --> 00:11:55.440
<i>Petty tricks won't work on him either.{小細工は聞かねぇ}</i>

00:11:56.860 --> 00:11:58.200
"The supple Kaguya..."{なよ輝夜 皇子御家(みこみや)つ子が 春の夢}{see: kaguya-hime}

00:11:59.490 --> 00:12:02.820
"You were an ephemeral dream to more than the princes."

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:07.320
Kaguya

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:15.750
Is that all there is to the Dragon's Right Eye?

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:22.980
Oyakata-sama!

00:12:22.980 --> 00:12:24.970
What has happened?

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:29.860
Oyakata-sama!

00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:37.670
As I'd expect from the God of War.

00:12:37.670 --> 00:12:38.700
You are strong indeed.

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:42.700
Will you listen to my last request?

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:47.870
In exchange for the life of Date's 
second-in-command, Katakura Kojuurou,

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:49.990
will you let the rest of my party go?

00:12:54.350 --> 00:12:57.460
Don't try to run away through death.

00:12:57.460 --> 00:12:59.980
Right now, you are not a commander. {lit. right now you are not a commander. nor are you the dragon's right eye.}

00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:02.510
Nor are you the Dragon's Right Eye.

00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:05.660
And a crowd without a commander is not an army.{将なき群れは軍にあらず}

00:13:06.740 --> 00:13:08.800
You are not worth fighting.

00:13:21.980 --> 00:13:23.570
All right, come on!

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:26.570
We've got to last until Master Sanada returns!

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:27.490
What now?

00:13:29.050 --> 00:13:30.990
The strongest man in the land? Here, now?

00:13:35.470 --> 00:13:37.400
That's got to be against the rules.

00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:39.380
Let me have a shot!

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:40.880
Master Shimazu!

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:42.710
You're a guest!

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:45.800
I'm better suited to fight him than you are.

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:47.630
Come on, it's you and me!

00:13:49.730 --> 00:13:51.510
What is Master Sanada doing?!

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:58.270
Oyakata-sama...

00:13:58.270 --> 00:14:00.200
Oyakata-sama!

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:03.730
Yukimura!

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:06.280
O-Oyakata-sama!

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:10.030
Oyakata-sama...

00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:12.030
Oyakata-sa—

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:13.530
Listen to me!

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:19.420
Oyakata-sama.

00:14:23.310 --> 00:14:25.130
Yukimura...

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:28.820
I'm here.

00:14:28.820 --> 00:14:30.340
Takeda's...

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:33.980
Takeda's future...

00:14:34.660 --> 00:14:37.060
I leave it...

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:38.540
to you...

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:41.050
Yukimura...

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:44.270
It's in your hands.

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:48.150
Oyakata-sama.

00:14:51.110 --> 00:14:55.590
Oyakata-sama! Oyakata-sama!

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:59.960
What are you doing, Master Sanada?!

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:02.250
Both the left and right flanks are falling apart out there! {check}{右翼も左翼も総崩れだ}

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:03.340
At this rate...

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:05.260
Oyakata-sama is...

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:08.030
Wha—

00:15:07.640 --> 00:15:10.760
Oyakata-sama! Oyakata-sama! {overlap}

00:15:08.030 --> 00:15:09.930
This is bad.

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:13.970
Oyakata-sama! Oyakata-sama!

00:15:15.920 --> 00:15:17.190
All forces, retreat!

00:15:17.190 --> 00:15:18.900
Retreat!

00:15:24.020 --> 00:15:25.650
You're not bad.

00:15:27.660 --> 00:15:29.030
Retreat?

00:15:29.790 --> 00:15:32.660
Wait, Tadakatsu!

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:39.130
Ieyasu, why is Takeda retreating?

00:15:39.130 --> 00:15:40.290
No idea.

00:15:40.680 --> 00:15:43.300
<i>Takeda shouldn't be this weak.</i>

00:15:44.300 --> 00:15:46.200
Shikoku

00:15:49.110 --> 00:15:51.260
There's a bad wind blowing.

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:52.720
Nakatomigawa

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:03.960
You guys!

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:05.100
Shige!

00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:06.270
Bekunosuke! {is that sound right?}{yes}

00:16:09.300 --> 00:16:10.830
What's all this?

00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:12.750
A-Aniki...{pls}

00:16:12.750 --> 00:16:13.740
Yosu! {?}{*check credits}

00:16:14.740 --> 00:16:16.840
What the hell happened?

00:16:16.840 --> 00:16:19.090
I-It was Tokugawa...

00:16:19.090 --> 00:16:20.250
Tokugawa?

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:26.330
Sorry... We couldn't hold while you were gone...

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:28.130
H-Hey!

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:30.050
Snap out of it! Hey!

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:36.760
Ie... yasu?

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:43.950
You're pretty good.

00:16:43.950 --> 00:16:45.090
You, too.

00:16:46.600 --> 00:16:49.910
Hey, how about we partner up?

00:16:49.910 --> 00:16:52.640
It's better than destroying each other.

00:16:55.130 --> 00:16:57.780
All right, I'll trust you.

00:16:57.780 --> 00:17:01.100
Huh? You're gonna trust me?

00:17:01.100 --> 00:17:03.510
You proposed it, so what's the problem?

00:17:03.510 --> 00:17:07.420
Well, ya know, we just met.

00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:10.440
Is it all right to trust somebody so quickly?

00:17:10.440 --> 00:17:14.300
I can tell whether I should trust you by looking at your men.

00:17:14.300 --> 00:17:17.260
You're a man who doesn't betray others.

00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:23.640
Why...?

00:17:23.640 --> 00:17:26.650
I-Ieyasu!

00:17:27.850 --> 00:17:32.070
What... the hell?!

00:17:29.570 --> 00:17:32.070
Chousokabe     Motochika

00:17:29.570 --> 00:17:32.070
Chousokabe     Motochika

00:17:33.010 --> 00:17:34.440
You're late.

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:38.340
Sorry.

00:17:38.340 --> 00:17:41.500
I've been busy running around in all directions.

00:17:41.500 --> 00:17:45.690
You've done well to raise your stature in the midst of this chaos.

00:17:45.690 --> 00:17:47.790
I have no idea what you're talking about,

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:49.590
my comrade.

00:17:49.600 --> 00:17:51.840
Mouri Motonari

00:17:52.040 --> 00:17:53.420
Toyotomi perished in battle,

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:54.840
Takenaka has fallen.

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:57.540
The one who had the most to gain is you. {check}{good}

00:18:00.230 --> 00:18:01.810
Well, it matters not.

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:06.230
What matters is how you will act from this point on.

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:10.110
If we make known all of Tokugawa's atrocities,

00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:13.160
and emphasize that justice lies with us,

00:18:13.160 --> 00:18:16.360
many will gather to our side.

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:18.670
Tokugawa's "atrocities"?

00:18:18.670 --> 00:18:19.990
Can you honestly say such a thing?

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:24.810
Why, it's only natural to assume that Tokugawa would attempt to subjugate Chousokabe.

00:18:24.810 --> 00:18:27.740
People do not believe in the truth;

00:18:27.740 --> 00:18:32.000
they make up convenient truths from what they see.

00:18:33.290 --> 00:18:34.540
<i>Ootani.</i>

00:18:34.540 --> 00:18:38.220
<i>Chousokabe, Ishida, Tokugawa.</i>

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:41.320
<i>I don't care about your motives.</i>

00:18:41.830 --> 00:18:44.550
<i>Whoever wants to rule this country can have it.</i>

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:47.870
I have only one goal:

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:49.690
the stability of my province.

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:53.690
Everything I do is to secure my rule.

00:18:55.660 --> 00:18:57.640
What happened to Takeda?

00:18:57.640 --> 00:18:58.760
Lord Shingen...

00:18:58.760 --> 00:18:59.700
Ieyasu.

00:19:00.540 --> 00:19:04.490
Our scouts can't find any ambushes or traps. {check}{伏兵も罠も}

00:19:04.840 --> 00:19:06.670
This is the perfect time to chase them.

00:19:06.670 --> 00:19:07.630
What will you do?

00:19:08.320 --> 00:19:09.080
Wait!

00:19:10.870 --> 00:19:12.230
What...

00:19:12.230 --> 00:19:13.090
is that?!

00:19:15.730 --> 00:19:18.220
Withdraw! Run away from that maelstrom!

00:19:20.140 --> 00:19:23.100
I've found you, Oichi-sama.

00:19:23.100 --> 00:19:25.500
Tenkai

00:19:23.990 --> 00:19:25.510
Tenkai-sama!

00:19:25.970 --> 00:19:28.230
Let's have mushroom stew for dinner!

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:29.900
Kobayakawa Hideaki

00:19:30.590 --> 00:19:34.600
<i>{singing}A thousand miles</i>

00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:38.300
<i>in search...{wut}{尋ね訪ねて 幾千里}</i>

00:19:34.790 --> 00:19:35.570
That is...

00:19:39.450 --> 00:19:44.570
Ah, life is fading away.

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:46.580
Oichi

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:46.580
.

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:46.580
.

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:46.580
.

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:46.580
.

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:49.850
Could that be Oichi-dono?

00:19:49.850 --> 00:19:52.020
Oda Nobunaga's little sister?

00:19:52.780 --> 00:19:54.080
She was alive?

00:19:54.800 --> 00:19:57.590
Who are you?

00:20:02.270 --> 00:20:03.800
You are...

00:20:05.100 --> 00:20:06.630
too bright.

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:12.810
Ieyasu!

00:20:17.960 --> 00:20:19.720
What's over there?

00:20:19.720 --> 00:20:21.320
It's very dark.

00:20:25.580 --> 00:20:31.410
As light and dark melt and mix together, nothingness is born.{虚無}

00:20:47.090 --> 00:20:48.450
Kenshin-sama,

00:20:48.450 --> 00:20:49.640
Takeda Shingen has...

00:20:51.460 --> 00:20:54.510
collapsed from illness at the height of battle.

00:20:54.670 --> 00:20:58.660
<i>His connection to this world now wavers between dream and reality.</i>

00:20:58.660 --> 00:21:04.960
<i>The heavens have shown we are helpless against the coming war.{天はこれより起こる戦乱に私たちはmuyuu?と示したのですね}</i>

00:21:10.450 --> 00:21:11.780
It's the castle!

00:21:11.780 --> 00:21:13.260
I can see the castle!

00:21:13.260 --> 00:21:14.790
We're home!

00:21:17.260 --> 00:21:20.620
Ishida... Mitsunari.

